       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/6d51465aa828084aeddbf6d03c81fdc4?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAW-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Andrew Woods",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>There are two options:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>If you want the server managed triples from the memento, you must restart Fedora in \"relaxed\" mode:<br/>\n<a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA5x/Configuration+Options+Inventory#ConfigurationOptionsInventory-Allowinguserupdatestocertainservermanagedtriples\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA5x/Configuration+Options+Inventory#ConfigurationOptionsInventory-Allowinguserupdatestocertainservermanagedtriples</a></li>\n\t<li>Or, if you do not need the SMTs to be the same as what is in the memento, you can use \"Prefere: handling=lenient\"<br/>\n<a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA5x/RESTful+HTTP+API+-+Containers#RESTfulHTTPAPI-Containers-YellowPUTCreatearesourcewithaspecifiedpath,orreplacethetriplesassociatedwitharesourcewiththetriplesprovidedintherequestbody\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA5x/RESTful+HTTP+API+-+Containers#RESTfulHTTPAPI-Containers-YellowPUTCreatearesourcewithaspecifiedpath,orreplacethetriplesassociatedwitharesourcewiththetriplesprovidedintherequestbody</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n",
     "created": "07/Jan/19 12:07 PM",
